        <definition>void DatabaseConnectionPool::reconnect_all</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>reconnect_all</name>
        <qualifiedname>DatabaseConnectionPool::reconnect_all</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Reconnects every idle connection in parallel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reconnects all currently idle connections in parallel.</para>
<para>Holds the pool lock for the whole operation so no idle connection can be handed out while it is being reconnected; busy connections are not touched.</para>
<para>Uses forEachIdle to hold the pool lock while the reconnect tasks run and until every task has been waited on, so no idle connection is handed out half-way through a reconnect. Busy (already leased) connections are not touched here. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Each reconnect&apos;s success or failure (including exceptions) is logged; the method itself does not throw for an individual connection failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
