    <briefdescription>
<para>Owns the fixed set of synchronous <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> connections and leases them to callers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Connections are created in parallel at construction and stored in a <ref refid="classBlockingPool" kindref="compound">BlockingPool</ref>. Callers obtain a connection with <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a39716826b3e5be2f15603d8cf809446b" kindref="member">get_connection()</ref> and must give it back with <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1ace8c17b9fea41e732a18f9700af847bb" kindref="member">return_connection()</ref>; in practice <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> does this via RAII. The acquire timeout is read once from configuration at startup. When a wait for a connection expires, <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a39716826b3e5be2f15603d8cf809446b" kindref="member">get_connection()</ref> throws <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref>, which the HTTP layer maps to 503.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: connection hand-out and return are serialised by <ref refid="classBlockingPool" kindref="compound">BlockingPool</ref>; the slow-wait warning rate limiter is atomic. Non-copyable and non-movable. <simplesect kind="warning"><para>A failed initialisation is fatal: the constructor logs and calls <computeroutput>exit(EXIT_FAILURE)</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classBlockingPool" kindref="compound">BlockingPool</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
